        "expansion_item_XiQ3CN": {
          "type": "expansion_item",
          "name": "Official Rules",
          "settings": {
            "button_title": "Official Rules",
            "button_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "button_bg_color": "#000000",
            "expand_text": "<p><strong>THRILLJOY PIX! </strong><em><strong>POST MALONE</strong></em><strong> SWEEPSTAKES&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>OFFICIAL RULES</strong></p><p><strong>NO PURCHASE OR PAYMENT OF ANY KIND IS NECESSARY TO ENTER OR WIN. A PURCHASE OR PAYMENT WILL NOT IMPROVE YOUR CHANCES OF WINNING. VOID WHERE PROHIBITED.</strong></p><p><strong>1. Sponsor</strong></p><p>This Thrilljoy PIX! <em>Post Malone</em> Sweepstakes (the “Sweepstakes”) is sponsored by Thrilljoy, LLC, 7401 Laurel Canyon Blvd., Suite 22, North Hollywood, CA 91605. (“Sponsor” or “Thrilljoy”).</p><p><strong>2. Eligibility</strong></p><p>The Sweepstakes is open only to legal residents of the fifty (50) United States and the District of Columbia who are eighteen (18) years of age or older as of the date of entry. Void where prohibited or restricted by law. Employees, officers, directors, and agents of Sponsor and its affiliates, subsidiaries, and advertising and promotion agencies, and the immediate family and household members of each, are not eligible. “Immediate family members” shall mean parents, step-parents, children, step-children, siblings, step-siblings, or spouses, regardless of where they live. &nbsp;“Household members” shall mean people who share the same residence at least three (3) months a year, whether related or not. By entering, each entrant agrees to be bound by these Official Rules and by the decisions of Sponsor, which are final and binding on all matters relating to the Sweepstakes.</p><p><strong>3. Promotion Period</strong></p><p>The Sweepstakes begins on November 13, 2026 at 12:00:01 a.m. Pacific Time (“PT”) and ends on December 18, 2026 at 11:59:59 p.m. PT (the “Promotion Period”). Sponsor’s computer is the official time-keeping device for the Sweepstakes.</p><p><strong>4. How to Enter — No Purchase or Payment Necessary</strong></p><p><strong>(a) Free online entry. </strong>During the Promotion Period, visit https://thrilljoy.com/pages/sweepstakes and complete and submit the entry form, including your name, email address, and any other required fields. This method of entry is free; no purchase or payment of any kind is required. Although it is free to enter, standard data rates and charges may be incurred if you use your mobile device to enter the Sweepstakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>(b) Entry limit. </strong>Limit one entry per person during the Promotion Period. No entry fee, payment, shipping or handling charge, paid application or subscription, proof of purchase, mandatory survey, paid account, or other thing of value is required to enter or to win. Entries by the same person in excess of the limits stated herein will be disqualified. Entries will be deemed to have been submitted by the authorized account holder of the email address submitted with entry. “Authorized account holder” is defined as the natural person who is assigned to an email address by an Internet access provider, online service provider or organization (e.g., business, educational institution, etc.) that is responsible for assigning email addresses for the domain associated with the submitted email address. Entering or attempting to enter the Sweepstakes multiple times through the use of multiple email addresses is prohibited and any such entries will be deemed void and disqualified. All submissions become the property of Sponsor upon receipt and will not be acknowledged or returned.</p><p><strong>(c) Equal treatment. </strong>All entries, regardless of method, have equal dignity and an equal chance of winning. No method of entry will be given any advantage or disadvantage in the selection of winners. All entries become the property of Sponsor and will not be returned. Entries that are incomplete, illegible, or generated by automated or unauthorized means are void.</p><p><strong>5. Prizes.</strong> One prize will be awarded. The prize consists of one (1) merchandise pack, one (1) Expedia gift card with an approximate retail value (\"ARV\") of One Thousand U.S. Dollars (US$1,000), two (2) tickets to a Post Malone show (the “Concert”), and a meet-and-greet opportunity with Post Malone (the “Meet & Greet”). The aggregate ARV of all prizes in this Sweepstakes is $5,000 USD. Merchandise pack contents and content quantity shall be determined by Sponsor in its discretion. Expedia gift card is subject to its terms and conditions, is not redeemable for cash value, and will not be replaced if lost or stolen.</p><p>For the Concert: Seat assignment and location will be as selected by Sponsor in its discretion and is subject to availability and change. Concert tickets are subject to their terms and conditions and will not be replaced if lost or stolen; they may also be subject to any restrictions, terms or conditions of the Concert venue. Winner and guest must comply with all regulations, laws, rules, policies and requirements applicable to the Concert and its venue. Winner and winner’s guest must be available for the Concert on the designated date/time; alternate dates/times are not available. Sponsor is not responsible if the Concert is delayed, postponed, or cancelled for any reason, and winner will not be reimbursed for the value of the tickets. Sponsor is not responsible if winner does not use the tickets to attend the Concert; no compensation will be awarded in lieu thereof. Concert tickets awarded are for winner’s personal use only and may not be sold or offered for resale or used for any commercial purpose. Any such resale or commercial use may result in disqualification of winner and forfeiture of prize.&nbsp;</p><p>For the Meet & Greet: The Meet & Greet is subject to Post Malone’s schedule and availability and may be subject to cancellation. Neither the Sponsor nor Austin Richard Post p/k/a/ Post Malone, Posty Touring, Inc., AP Group Holdings, LLC &nbsp;and their respective parent companies, subsidiaries, affiliates, promotion agencies and agents and each of their respective directors, officers, employees and assigns, promotion agencies and agents are responsible if the Meet & Greet is unavailable, delayed, postponed, cancelled, or rescheduled, in whole or in part, for any reason. No compensation or substitution of prize component will be paid in lieu of a cancelled appearance as this portion of the prize has no cash value. Winner and winner’s guest must be available to attend the Meet & Greet on its scheduled day, time and location. Winner and winner’s guest must follow and adhere to all applicable rules, regulations or directives of Sponsor and/or its designee in connection with the Meet & Greet opportunity.</p><p>In the event that winner and/or winner’s guest may be intoxicated, or engages in behavior that, as determined by Sponsor, its designee or Concert venue/personnel in their sole discretion, is unruly, obnoxious or threatening, a safety risk, illegal or otherwise inappropriate or that is intended to annoy, abuse, threaten or harass any other person, Sponsor reserves the right to revoke full or partial prize from winner or winner’s guest, terminate the participation of winner and/or winner’s guest in the Concert and/or Meet & Greet, as applicable, or take such other action as it may deem necessary and appropriate in its discretion.</p><p>Winner’s guest must be a legal fifty (50) U.S./D.C. resident and at least eighteen (18) years of age. In Sponsor’s discretion, winner’s guest may be required to sign and return to Sponsor a release of liability/publicity release (where permitted by law) prior to award of prize to winner or such guest may not be permitted to accompany winner and that portion of the prize will be forfeited. If winner’s guest is a minor in their legal state of residence, the release must be signed by such guest’s parent/legal guardian on their behalf.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>If Sponsor elects, potential winner and winner’s guest may be required to submit to a confidential background check. &nbsp;Such background check may include (but is not limited to) investigation of criminal, sexual offenses, or other arrest or conviction record, and any other factor deemed relevant by the Sponsor to help ensure that the potential winner and winner’s guest will not bring the Sponsor, Austin Richard Post p/k/a Post Malone, Posty Touring, Inc., Posty Posts, Inc., or AP Group Holdings, LLC into public disrepute, contempt, scandal or ridicule or reflect unfavorably on the Sponsor, Austin Richard Post p/k/a Post Malone, Posty Touring, Inc., Posty Posts, Inc., or AP Group Holdings, LLC. &nbsp;If requested, the potential winner and winner’s guest agree to sign waiver forms authorizing the release of personal and background information. &nbsp;In the event of noncompliance, to be determined at the sole discretion of Sponsor, prize will be forfeited, and an alternate potential winner may be randomly selected in Sponsor’s discretion and time permitting.</p><p>Prize includes only the components specified and described in these Official Rules; any and all other costs and expenses not specifically mentioned herein are solely winner’s responsibility.</p><p>Prizes are non-transferable. No prize substitution or cash equivalent is permitted except by Sponsor, which reserves the right to substitute a prize of equal or greater value if an advertised prize becomes unavailable. Limit one (1) prize per person. All prize details not specified in these Official Rules are at Sponsor’s sole discretion.</p><p><strong>6. Odds of Winning</strong></p><p>The odds of winning depend on the number of eligible entries received during the Promotion Period.</p><p><strong>7. Winner Selection</strong></p><p>One winner will be selected in a random drawing from among all eligible entries received during the Promotion Period. The drawing will be conducted on December 21, 2026 by Sponsor, whose decisions are final and binding.</p><p><strong>8. Winner Notification; Claim Deadline; Unclaimed Prizes</strong></p><p>Potential winner will be notified by email using the contact information provided at entry, on or about December 21, 2026. Potential winner will be required to complete, sign, and return an affidavit of eligibility, including, without limitation, a liability release, and (where lawful) a publicity release (collectively the “Affidavit”) within ten (10) days of the date of notification. If winner is under the age of majority in its state of legal residence, the Affidavit must be signed by the winner’s parent or legal guardian on its behalf. The contents and requirements of the foregoing affidavit will be at Sponsor’s discretion. If a potential winner cannot be contacted within five (5) days, fails to respond or return required documents by the stated deadline, is found ineligible, or declines the prize, the prize may be forfeited and an alternate winner may be selected at random from among the remaining eligible entries, at Sponsor’s discretion and time permitting.</p><p><strong>9. Taxes</strong></p><p>All prizes are awarded “as is.” The winner is solely responsible for all federal, state, and local taxes associated with the receipt or use of a prize. For any prize with an ARV of $2,000600 or more, the winner will be required to complete and return an IRS Form W-9 before the prize is awarded, and Sponsor will issue an IRS Form 1099 to the winner and to the IRS as required by law.</p><p><strong>10. Publicity / Likeness Release</strong></p><p>Except where prohibited by law, acceptance of a prize constitutes the winner’s consent for Sponsor to use the winner’s name, city and state of residence, and likeness for advertising and promotional purposes without further notice or compensation. Residents of Tennessee and New York: Sponsor will obtain any additional consent required by applicable law prior to such use, including written consent where required.</p><p><strong>11. Release; Limitation of Liability; Indemnification</strong></p><p>By entering, each entrant agrees to release, indemnify, and hold harmless Sponsor, Austin Richard Post p/k/a Post Malone, Posty Touring, Inc., Posty Posts, Inc., and AP Group Holdings, LLC, and each of their respective parent, subsidiary and affiliated companies and their respective officers, directors, employees, representatives and agents, from and against any liability, injury, loss, or damage of any kind arising from participation in the Sweepstakes or in any Sweepstakes-related or prize-related activity, or from the acceptance, possession, or use of any prize. Sponsor is not responsible for lost, late, misdirected, garbled, incomplete, or undeliverable entries or notifications, or for any technical, hardware, software, network, or other failure of any kind.</p><p><strong>12. Disputes; Governing Law</strong></p><p>Except where prohibited, each entrant agrees that: (a) any and all disputes, claims, and causes of action arising out of or connected with the Sweepstakes or any prize awarded shall be resolved individually, without resort to any form of class action; (b) any and all claims, judgments, and awards shall be limited to actual out-of-pocket costs incurred, including costs associated with entering the Sweepstakes, but in no event attorneys’ fees; and (c) under no circumstances will an entrant be permitted to obtain awards for, and each entrant hereby waives all rights to claim, punitive, incidental, and consequential damages and any other damages, other than for actual out-of-pocket expenses, and any and all rights to have damages multiplied or otherwise increased. These Official Rules and the Sweepstakes are governed by, and construed in accordance with, the laws of the State of California, without giving effect to any choice-of-law or conflict-of-law rules. By entering, each entrant consents to the jurisdiction and venue of the federal and state courts located in Los Angeles, California, for any disputes arising out of these Official Rules or the Sweepstakes, and waive any claim of forum non conveniens or lack of personal jurisdiction that they may have.</p><p><strong>13. Privacy</strong></p><p>Personal information collected from entrants is subject to Sponsor’s Privacy Policy, available at <a href=\"https://thrilljoy.com/policies/privacy-policy\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">https://thrilljoy.com/policies/privacy-policy</span></a>. Sponsor provides notice at the point of entry of the categories of personal information collected and will use that information only to administer the Sweepstakes unless the entrant consents otherwise. California residents and residents of other states with applicable privacy laws have the data rights described in the Privacy Policy.</p><p><strong>14. Winners List and Copy of Official Rules</strong></p><p>For a copy of these Official Rules or a list of winners (available after December 21, 2026, send a self-addressed, stamped envelope to Thrilljoy, LLC, 7401 Laurel Canyon Blvd., Suite 22, North Hollywood, CA 91605 by October 31, 2026. Vermont residents may omit return postage.</p><p><strong>15. Social Media / Platform Release</strong></p><p>If the Sweepstakes is promoted or entered through any third-party platform, the Sweepstakes is in no way sponsored, endorsed, administered by, or associated with such platform. Entrants must comply with all applicable platform terms, and a free, non-social method of entry remains available as described in Section 4.</p><p>Acknowledgement: &nbsp;Entrants acknowledge and agree that neither Austin Richard Post p/k/a Post Malone, Posty Touring, Inc., Posty Posts, Inc., AP Group Holdings, LLC, nor any of their respective subsidiaries, affiliates, owners, officers, directors, employees, agents or representatives, are responsible in any manner whatsoever for the administration, implementation or operation of or for the Sweepstakes, and none are prize providers with regard hereto.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
          }
        },
